Reach slicc-kernel's network and file modes from the Fastly CLI on wasip1.

Reason: wasip1 cannot dial, so every API call fails at DNS. pkg/slicchost
talks to host/fastly-host.mjs (fastly_host probe/call/take) and sets
http.DefaultTransport to it; the CLI's own client, the update and log-tail
clients and auth's token requests use that transport. go-fastly builds its
own http.Transport, so on wasip1 its client takes http.DefaultTransport
instead. Requests and response bodies cross as JSON; each body read yields
to other goroutines first. wasip1 mkdir and open pass no mode and wasip1
chmod does nothing, so the config directory (0700), config.toml (0600,
it holds API tokens) and errors.log (0600, it records command lines,
--token included) are set through the host's chmod. text.InputSecure reads
a line when stdin is not a terminal (term.ReadPassword fails on a pipe,
and wasip1 has no terminal ioctls), so `fastly auth login` takes a pasted
or piped token. Without the host module, HTTP fails with "it needs
slicc-kernel with @ai-ecoverse/wasi-fastly's host module" and the modes
are left alone.

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: wasip1 can dial and set file modes without a host module.

